MAJOR_VERSION=4
STANDARD_VERSION=2
RELEASE_VERSION=0
PRERELEASE=1
DEV_VERSION=15
DESCRIPTION<<VER_END
PRE 4.2.0: WSL server host UAC gate — press any key and deferred hosting line

- server host on WSL: yellow elevation NOTICE plus "Press any key to continue..."
  before the Windows UAC prompt; "[Server] hosting as ..." prints only after
  portproxy setup succeeds (or bridge fallback succeeds)
- server kill / leave / exit: same press-any-key gate before portproxy teardown UAC
- interactive shell: Ctrl+C on an empty input line returns to a fresh shell> prompt
- interactive shell: Ctrl+C cancels in-flight commands (BATCH_SINGLE_THREAD too); empty-line
  ^C no longer toggles raw mode off/on
- press-any-key NOTICE gate: ^C prints a new line and re-prompts without aborting host,
  kill, or portproxy teardown; threadpool gate suppresses command cancel during the gate
- exit / server leave / server kill: always run WSL portproxy+firewall teardown when active
  (exit hook registered via atexit as well as explicit exit command)
- review fixes: keypress waits release session_mutex first; tcsetattr failure and
  non-TTY stdin no longer bypass or block the gate; WSL-local hosting survives LAN
  exposure failure when defer_hosting defers the success line
- server host on WSL: probe Windows portproxy/firewall via server-proxy-check
  before NOTICE/UAC when portproxy elevation is required (not a TCP bind probe)
- FlinstonePowershell server-proxy: netsh-only via elevated cmd.exe (no temp
  PowerShell scripts or New-NetFirewallRule module load) for faster UAC apply
VER_END

RELEASE_DATE=2026-06-17
